@startuml humidityPackage
title The ventilation law with the gh#84 package: stepped v2 and graded v2\n(the prototype in model/closedloop/humidity_prototype.py: green is what the package adds or changes, blue is stepped v1 and graded v1 as shipped)

' One call of the law, as T6 makes it every poll. Green is what the package
' adds or changes; blue is drivers/ventModel as shipped (2.14.1). Mode 2's law
' (graded) embeds the stepped law, so everything down to "Windows" is shared
' by both modes, and so is the package.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam wrapWidth 330
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #E8F1FB
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #2C5AA0
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #2C5AA0
skinparam ArrowColor #2C3E50
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #7F8C8D
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FEFDE8
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C8B400
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam LegendBorderColor #7F8C8D

start
:T6 calls the law every poll (30 s):
T_avg and RH_avg (T5's averages; T_avg in whole °C for the ladder),
the day or night setpoints, and the windows' states;

if (temperature reading valid?) then (no)
  :hold every window
  (reason NO_DATA);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

partition "Temperature branch (unchanged)" {
  :step_t = ceil((T_avg − t_max) / max(hyst_t / 3, 1)), 0 to 3
  close guard: once venting, hold step 1 until T_avg ≤ t_max − hyst_t;
}

partition "Humidity branch" {
  if (humidity control on and RH valid?) then (no)
    :step_rh = no vote;
  elseif (RH_avg > rh_max?) then (yes)
    :step_rh = ceil((RH_avg − rh_max) / max(hyst_rh / 3, 1)), 1 to 3;
  elseif (last vote > 0 and RH_avg > rh_max − max(hyst_rh / 3, 1)?) then (yes)
    :**close guard**
    step_rh = 1, held until RH_avg ≤ rh_max − max(hyst_rh / 3, 1); <<#DCEEDC>>
  elseif (RH_avg < rh_min?) then (yes)
    :step_rh = 0, "too dry"
    //under rule 1 this can no longer change any decision//;
  else (no)
    :step_rh = no vote;
  endif
}

partition "Resolve the two votes" {
  if (humidity has no vote?) then (yes)
    :step = step_t;
  elseif (both want to open (step_t > 0 and step_rh > 0)?) then (yes)
    :step = the higher of the two
    (humidity raises a step the temperature asked for);
  elseif (step_t = step_rh?) then (yes)
    :step = step_t;
  elseif (too dry while the temperature wants to vent\n(step_t > 0 and step_rh = 0)?) then (yes)
    :**rule 1, gh#84**
    step = step_t: dryness never closes against heat,
    under every priority; <<#DCEEDC>>
  else (humidity alone wants to open)
    if (cr_priority?) then (0)
      :step = 0
      (temperature first, unchanged);
    else (1 or 2, which now mean the same)
      if (floor: T_avg ≥ t_min + 2,\nor a humidity-only opening is live and T_avg ≥ t_min + 1?) then (yes)
        :**floor and cap**
        step = min(step_rh, 1): M1 only; <<#DCEEDC>>
      else (no)
        :**floor**
        step = 0; <<#DCEEDC>>
      endif
    endif
  endif
}

partition "Windows" {
  :M1 open from step 1, M2 from step 2;
  if (M3 linear, with a trusted position (mode 2, graded)?) then (no: mode 1)
    :M3 open at step 3;
  else (yes)
    if (step ≥ 2?) then (yes)
      :want = the larger of
      the temperature aperture (0 % at t_max + 1.5 °C, 100 % at + 3.5 °C)
      and humidity's demand (100 % at step_rh 3, else 0);
    else (no)
      :want = 0
      (humidity on its own never reaches M3);
    endif
    :rate limit: move only for a 10 % correction or to an end,
    at most 25 % per move, not within 10 minutes of the last drive;
  endif
}
stop

legend right
  <back:#DCEEDC>  new in the package  </back>    <back:#E8F1FB>  the shipped law, unchanged  </back>
  The package's constants are provisional: floor margin 2 °C,
  the floor's hysteresis 1 °C, the cap at step 1.
  The prototype compiles t_min in; the firmware adds it to vent_in_t.
  Acceptance: humidityControl.md, "The package, prototyped".
endlegend
@enduml
